      <title>Malcolm X – World Wide Revolution</title>
      <link>https://example.org/catalogue/docs/malcolm-x-speech/malcolm-x-speech/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 03 Apr 1964 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://example.org/catalogue/docs/malcolm-x-speech/malcolm-x-speech/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;h2&gt;Summary&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;summary&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#summary&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;In this 1965 speech, Malcolm X discusses the interconnectedness of global liberation movements and the fight for civil rights in the United States. He frames Black struggles within the broader context of anti-colonial resistance and international human rights.&lt;/p&gt;
